      "problem": "${J}_{1}(9)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{2}(3)=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, recall the following:\n\n- ${J}_{1}(9)$ represents a $1\\times 1$ Jordan block with $9$'s on the leading diagonal,\n\n- ${J}_{2}(3)$ represents a $2\\times 2$ Jordan block with $3$'s on the leading diagonal.\n\nTherefore, our Jordan blocks are given by\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(9)=[\\begin{aligned}9\\end{aligned}],\\,{J}_{2}(3)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe composition of our Jordan blocks gives the following block diagonal matrix:\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(9)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{2}(3)=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
